    (Q.trz_inaugurated ? 2 : 0);
Q.news_headline =
    "Lewica demands the Czajka contracts, tests and repair timetable";
!}

Our MPs cannot repair Warsaw's collector, so they demand the things they can
actually obtain: the failure reports, procurement record, daily water tests
and a dated temporary-pipeline plan. Engineers and river communities get the
microphone before party spokespeople.

The record does not rescue KO. A second failure remains a second failure, and
Trzaskowski still has to explain the system he supervised. It does stop our
criticism from becoming another version of the lie.

