We decline. A governing majority that cannot pass its own leader's bill should
fall on it, and we are not the crutch that keeps it standing.

The fur farms stay open. Animal-welfare organisations that have worked with our
deputies for years publish a statement they clearly found painful to write, and
our own progressive current spends the autumn explaining a vote it does not
believe in.

