Q.news_headline =
    "The Left plays the Warsaw tape back to Konfederacja's anti-Russian voters";
!}

We do not lead with fascism, because that argument has been running since 2015
and it moves nobody who is not already persuaded. We lead with the tape: Europe
to Siberia, the third Rome, Moscow as the guardian of Christian civilisation,
said in Warsaw, to applause, in front of a Polish deputy who did not walk out.

[? if fiore_palace != "bosak": <span class="party-konf"><b>Krzysztof Bosak</b></span>'s people spend the
month explaining to their own base why their partner's guest of honour draws the
map through Moscow.?][? if fiore_palace = "bosak": The explaining has to be done
from the Palace, because the camp that hosted Fiore now holds it, and a president
cannot decline the question the way a deputy can.?]
The line lands because it is true and because it is national, and that is exactly
what our progressive organisers object to: we have won a week by arguing in the
register of the people we oppose, and we have said nothing at all about the man
convicted of belonging to an armed organisation.

